extraction_notes: "WB17 Warlords of Russia printed 71-72 (cache p072-p073, cache page = printed folio + 1), read off the text layer. Heading Russian Villager O.C.C. on printed 71, with the stat block headed Typical Villager/Farmer/Worker O.C.C. & NPC (also known as peasants, citizens, and the Russian People). OPTIONAL: the book says the data can be used as a guide for creating Non-Player Characters or as an optional player character. The entry ends on printed 72: its related-skill list runs down the left column to Wilderness: Any (+5%), and its Secondary Skills, Standard Equipment, Vehicle, Money and Cybernetics lines top the right column (cache p073 lines 52-72), where the text layer interleaves them with the Warlord Troops & Men at Arms material that follows. || GROUP: listed under Russian Adventurer O.C.C.s on printed 57; the entry states no S.D.C. base, so men_of_arms is false and occ_group is optional. || XP: the Villager ladder on the Experience Tables, printed 6, read off a render. || The entry prints NO O.C.C. bonuses, no Psionics line and no Secret Resources line; none is stored. Attribute requirements: none, so no attribute_requirements key. || SKILL READINGS: Speaks Native Language at 90% is Language: Native Tongue at 90. Lore: one of choice (+15%) is one pick from the catalog''s lore rows that fit the setting (the off-world and other-setting lores are left out of the list; a reading). Piloting: two of choice (+5%); no bonus for Horsemanship is stored as two Pilot picks at +5; the Horsemanship alternative at no bonus is in the note only, because one choice group carries one bonus. Animal Husbandry is stored at +5% (40); the +10% if a farmer or raises livestock is in the note. Sing or Dance is one pick from the two at +15. Hand to Hand: Basic to Expert costs TWO related skills and Martial Arts (or Assassin, if anarchist or evil) THREE, as printed across the page break of printed 71-72. Pilot Skills: any conventional types of vehicles and horsemanship, no robots, ships, aircraft or military vehicles: stored as Pilot minus the robot, ship, aircraft, spacecraft and military rows, with Horsemanship (its own catalog category) offered as General and Exotic Animals only. Ventriloquism is filed under Technical in the catalog and is reached by name through the Rogue only-list. Science: Astronomy and Math only is Astronomy, Mathematics: Basic and Mathematics: Advanced. Technical +10% to any animal related skills is not stored (Technical is a flat +5). Secondary skills: four at level one and one more at levels 3, 6, 9, 12 and 15. || MONEY: 1D6x10 credits stored (the text layer prints !D6xlO); the 2D4x10 credits worth of tradeable goods (2D4xlO) is in GM Notes. || EQUIPMENT not stored as rows: one M.D. weapon and two ancient weapons; pitchfork or blunt weapon, walking stick/staff or sword, shovel, tinted goggles, bedroll, a water skin, belt, boots and personal items have no catalog row and are in GM Notes. The armor is a choice of the catalog''s light and medium homemade suits for the printed 30-60 M.D.C. The bicycle or donkey is the Vehicle line and is in restrictions and GM Notes, not equipment."
